schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Anatomy of a good DAO proposal
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A seven-part structure for a governance proposal: (1) a clear, specific
    title, (2) a 2-3 sentence summary of what's proposed/costs/outcome, (3)
    background/context explaining the need and evidence, (4) a specification
    of exact deliverables/timeline/responsible parties, (5) a detailed budget
    breakdown, (6) measurable success criteria, and (7) a risks section with
    mitigations.
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Presented as the complete template structure the article recommends DAO
    members follow, paired with a "before you propose" stage (informal
    temperature check, coalition-building, preemptive objection-handling).
  adjacent_meanings:
    - Grant-application templates (title/summary/budget/timeline structures used in traditional funding contexts — not named in the article but structurally similar)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      The article distinguishes the *proposal document* structure from the
      *pre-proposal process* (temperature check, coalition-building) —
      framing proposal failure as usually a process failure ("proposal is
      unclear, poorly scoped, or doesn't address community concerns") rather
      than an idea-quality failure.
  tensions: []
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    None flagged — a generic governance-process template, not attributed to a
    specific tradition or community.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/proposal-writing.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
